PETSELFTEST1
# V5-04 memory-driven lines. Three pickups 6 s apart, then good morning.
# Every pickup / morning line asks MemoryPhraseSelector once and logs the
# answer: PET_MEMORY_PHRASE (a real memory: a like the child chose on a
# dial question, or yesterday's book) or PET_MEMORY_DECISION used=0 with
# the reason (no_memory, too_soon, quiet, day_limit). Which one depends on
# what this device's ledger remembers, so the scenario only requires that
# each trigger gets exactly one answer and that nothing is invented or
# fails; the cap, quiet hours and no-memory fallback are host-tested
# (tests/cpp/test_memory_phrases.cc). With a like in the ledger, the 2nd
# and 3rd pickup read reason=too_soon. No sound pack clips exist for slot
# lines, so a used line logs src=text and the plain line plays.
# Counted from "mark begin" (see tools/selftest_report.py).
# expect min:PET_MEMORY_ 4
# expect min:ctx=pickup_like 3
# expect min:ctx=morning_recap 1
# expect min:PET_MORNING_STAYED 1
# expect none:PET_PHRASE_FAILED 0
# expect none:PET_MORNING_FALLBACK 0
# expect none:PET_SELFTEST_ABORT 0
# expect selftest_done 1
# Quiet sounds while testing (RAM only, this boot).
volume 15
waitidle 60000
pet
wait 6000
# Normalize restored pet state to "home, neutral".
tap press 6000
hold press 1500 6000
# Safety net: a morning that is not touched would power off; this alarm
# wakes the board again.
alarm 60
mark begin
gesture pickup
wait 6000
gesture pickup
wait 6000
gesture pickup
wait 6000
# Good morning, then a dial touch keeps TuanTuan awake.
morning
wait 15000
tap down 6000
wait 4000
end
